Stray semicolons: a doubled ';;' after statements, a line of nothing but
semicolons, and a ';' alone. Empty statements are harmless in SSL; the
scenario records whether the formatter keeps or drops them and that
nothing else changes.
Suspected issue: the formatter moves each extra ';' onto a line of its own (';;;' becomes three lines of ';', and one lands indented inside the :IF body), multiplying empty statements into layout rather than keeping or dropping them; no catalog entry covers empty statements.
-- input.ssl --
:DECLARE nCount;;
nCount := 1;;
;;;
;
:IF nCount > 0;;
	nCount += 1;
:ENDIF;;
:RETURN nCount;
-- format --
:DECLARE nCount;
;
nCount := 1;
;
;
;
;
;
:IF nCount > 0;
	;
	nCount += 1;
:ENDIF;
;
:RETURN nCount;
-- diagnostics --
-- diagnostics [--strict --info] --
